  <!-- Section 7: Packaging -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Packaging and Branding for DTC Ecommerce Brands</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Packaging is completely ignored by competitor content, yet it's critical for ecommerce success. When a customer opens your package, that moment determines whether they post an unboxing photo on Instagram or quietly return the item. Wholesale packaging - polybags in bulk boxes - doesn't work for DTC. Your packaging is your physical brand touchpoint, and it directly impacts reviews and repeat purchases.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Woven neck labels are your most visible branding element. These are the tags inside the neck that display your brand name and logo. Costing $0.10-0.30 each, woven labels look premium and last the garment's lifetime. Unlike printed labels that fade after washing, woven labels maintain your brand presence through dozens of washes. Position them at the center back neck for maximum visibility. Include your website URL so customers can find you when others ask where they got the shirt.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Hang tags cost $0.05-0.15 and serve multiple purposes. They display pricing, product information, and branding. More importantly, hang tags are the first thing customers see when they pull your garment from the package. Design them to make an impression - thick cardstock, embossing, or foil stamping communicates quality. Include a QR code linking to your website or a special offer to drive repeat traffic.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Individual polybags cost $0.02-0.08 and serve practical and aesthetic purposes. They protect garments during shipping from moisture and dirt. For the customer, a clean polybag creates a professional unboxing experience. Nothing says "amateur" like a wrinkled, dusty shirt arriving loose in a box. Polybags also allow you to include care instructions and size information where the customer will see them.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Custom mailer boxes cost $0.80-2.50 but deliver disproportionate value. These branded shipping boxes turn delivery into an experience. Customers photograph and share custom boxes on social media - free marketing. The unboxing moment builds emotional connection and increases repeat purchase rates. For premium brands, custom mailers are essential. For budget-conscious startups, start with polybags and upgrade to boxes as you scale.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Care labels with QR codes are a growing trend. Traditional care labels are boring - QR codes make them interactive. Scan the code to see your brand story, styling tips, or a video of the garment being made. This turns a regulatory requirement into a marketing opportunity. The cost difference is minimal, but the engagement potential is significant. Early adoption positions your brand as innovative.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Tissue paper with branded stamp adds a premium touch for $0.03-0.08 per package. It's not necessary for every order, but for premium products or first-time customers, the extra effort matters. Tissue paper creates anticipation as the customer unwraps layers - like opening a gift. Small details like this differentiate your brand in a crowded market.
      </p>
      
